    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0098" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/597: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="10" xml:id="d3-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-07T19:00:00-05:00">January 7, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. 1. Under date January 6 Davis telegraphed from London as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the substance of telegram No. 34, printed on <ref target="#pg1"
                        >page 1</ref>.]</p>
                <p>2. Department has had no information from any other source indicating that there
                    are in progress negotiations such as Craigie described.</p>
                <p>3. Please cable Department your comments and any information pertinent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d3-f1" n="10" type="source" xml:id="d3-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram was sent on the same date to the Embassy in Japan as No. 2.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
